<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss OZ 1996 profit rises 11.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Swiss OZ 1996 profit rises 11.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996:</p>
<p>				   (million Sfr unless stated)</p>
<p> Group net profit	     33.061	    vs 29.642</p>
<p> Earnings per share, Sfr    55.10	     vs 49.40</p>
<p> Financial income	     28.972	    vs 22.880</p>
<p> Commissions		    15.141	    vs 17.688</p>
<p> Sharecapital		   6.00		vs 30.00</p>
<p> Consolidated reserves	161.898	   vs 126.840</p>
<p> Dividend, bearer, Sfr	30.00	     vs zero</p>
<p> Par value of shares, Sfr   10		  vs 50</p>
<p> Return on equity, pct	19.50	     vs 19.70</p>
<p>NOTE - OZ Holding, a brokerage that specialises in covered options on Swiss securities, is 53 percent owned by the BZ Group Holding.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
